<title>CANADA: Canada agency sets framework for TV competition.</title>
<headline>Canada agency sets framework for TV competition.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's telecommunications regulators said on Tuesday they have put forward a new framework to encourage competition in the television distribution market.</p>
<p>&quot;The new policies are designed to foster fair competition in the broadcast distribution market in a way that will benefit consumers and strengthen the presence of high-quality Canadian programming in our broadcasting system,&quot; the Canadian Radio-television and Telecommunications Commission said in a statement.</p>
</text>
